    "Scouting Notes": "Ruiz had 60 stolen bases in the minors by July 11th. That’s… A lot. \n He’s got 80 grade speed.\n There are definite concerns with the bat. \n He did not hit the ball with any authority in the majors (SSS alert), but the AAA sample isn't that much better.\n Does hit the ball at an ideal launch angle, hits a lot of line drives and often gets to his harder contact at that launch angle as well.\n There has been a lot of swing and miss in the past, but it's been much better in 2022.\n Concern with this comes here, he simply doesn't swing at breaking balls in the minors. Which works there. But in the majors, that can cause issues.\n His numbers with the Padres org this year were insane, but in a very hitter friendly environment.\n Extremely good bunter, which I'd never note unless it was really impressive. Will be a legitimate weapon for him to use to get on base.\n The defense in the outfield is ok, but nothing too special, reliant on speed. Mediocre arm as well.\n Right now he’s comfortably 4th in the AAA OF group for me, but might be the most likely to impact the major league team this season.\n This is less of a knock on him and more of a sign of how deep that group is at this moment.\n Likely a bottom of the order hitter with some surprising juice and a meh glove that can handle all 3 outfield spots. Chance to be a solid regular, more likely a good 4th OF.",
